➤ Why is the DAG (Directed Acyclic Graph) so important in Spark’s execution?
=> 2 types of operations perform in spark 1.Transformation 2.Action
=> The DAG (Directed Acyclic Graph) is a core concept in Apache Spark’s execution model because 
   it defines how Spark processes data in a distributed and fault-tolerant way.
=> Spark creates a DAG based on your transformations (e.g., map, filter, groupBy)
=> It analyzes and optimizes this graph before execution
=> Transformations are not executed immediately
=> Spark waits until an action (like count, collect) is triggered
=> Then it builds and executes the DAG
=> Allows lazy evaluation and pipelining of transformations


